family: set-cli
what: trap
transport: v3
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: common set-style SNMP statements (set snmp trap-group …, set snmp v3 …); RFC 3413 (target addresses, target parameters, notify) and RFC 3414 (USM)
does: Sends the device's SNMP traps to Woodshed (SNMPv3).
check: Search Events for type Traps after a change on the device; `woodshed snmp status` counts traps per device.
placeholders: <V3-USER> <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- The statements follow the SNMPv3 notification model (RFC 3413): a target address, its parameters, and a notify entry that ties them together by tag. The keywords for each piece differ between devices.
- Add the same user in Woodshed: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, name <V3-USER>, SHA-256 and AES-128, with the same passphrases.
- Some devices also need the trap categories chosen (link, chassis, configuration) before they send anything.
---- part cli "": Enter in configuration mode, then commit
set snmp v3 usm local-engine user <V3-USER> authentication-sha256 authentication-password <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
set snmp v3 usm local-engine user <V3-USER> privacy-aes128 privacy-password <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
set snmp v3 target-address woodshed address 192.0.2.10
set snmp v3 target-address woodshed port 162
set snmp v3 target-address woodshed tag-list woodshed-traps
set snmp v3 target-address woodshed target-parameters woodshed-params
set snmp v3 target-parameters woodshed-params parameters message-processing-model v3
set snmp v3 target-parameters woodshed-params parameters security-model usm
set snmp v3 target-parameters woodshed-params parameters security-level privacy
set snmp v3 target-parameters woodshed-params parameters security-name <V3-USER>
set snmp v3 notify woodshed-notify type trap tag woodshed-traps
commit
